by paper Eq.~(4):
\begin{equation}
N(t)\approx\Nsm(t)+\Nfl(t),\qquad
\Nfl(t)=-\frac1\pi\sum_{p\in P}\sum_{m=1}^{3}\frac{\sin(mt\log p)}{m\,p^{m/2}} ,
\label{eq:hilbert-polya-nfl}
\end{equation}
with $P$ a finite set of primes. The comparison with Gutzwiller's formula below concerns the untruncated formal sum $-\frac1\pi\sum_{p}\sum_{m=1}^{\infty}\sin(mt\log p)/(m\,p^{m/2})$, taken over all primes and all $m$. Eq.~\eqref{eq:hilbert-polya-nfl} is a truncation of that sum. Term by term the two are the same, so the dictionary can be read off from either.
